# S0: the AUDITED eight-seat 262k attach and exactness smoke on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-audit (the gate profile's audits plus the fused-commit and verify-glue audits, the nine levers, the two quad
# blocks, 19,968 pooled blocks under the reservation, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_SINGLES_AUDIT=all). Never attached on hardware. READ in this order and stop at the first failure: (1) 'packed-any admission passed ... capacity=262144', 'kv reservation
# installed' with the pool the profile states (num_gpu_blocks=19968), extent block engaged blocks=2; (2) the fused commit engaged on BOTH blocks (a refusal line per block is the finding to record),
# the verify-glue engaged markers; (3) ZERO audit mismatches (verify T1/T2, extent, fused commit, vglue, the draft singles audit: an equal=1 line for each of the groups [0, 1, 2, 3] and [4, 5, 6, 7]); (4) concurrent8_steady: exactly two quad markers (slots 0,1,2,3 and 4,5,6,7), a round both
# quads served, a '[PINDIAG] draft mask pooled' and '[PINDIAG] draft outputs pooled' line for each block's slots, no pooled-refused, fallback or disable line (a capture refusal by headroom is recorded with the free-DRAM figures: the quads are captured after the pool exists); (5) every answer's hash equal to S0c's (the 8x262k-gate control run in this pack) and to solo, and per request the accepted tokens and verify-round counts equal S0c's (a wrong draft only lowers acceptance: text alone cannot show the quads exact). Record the memory ledger's free DRAM per chip at eight live seats. CONVERSION: F8 is DEFINED on the 16,416-block pool and S0 allocates 19,968, so F8 = ledger free + (19,968 - 16,416) x 557,056 B = ledger free + 1.979 GB; the ledger reading itself must be at least 2.07 GB for 21,760 blocks (F8 >= 4.05 GB) and 1.08 GB for the stated 19,968 (F8 >= 3.06 GB). This reading is also the only measure of the verify-glue levers' and request-warm's DRAM (the pool arithmetic charges them nothing); the pool sits at the high-band edge (19,968 of 19,979 blocks), so a lower reading is a finding. The pool re-sets from F8. Duration (estimate): 120 min. Stop rule.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/262k8 eight-seat 262k development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/262k8 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-best-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/262k8 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-best-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent8_code,concurrent8_steady,concurrent5_split,concurrent8_drain
